126: /* Split for the same reason the colour reset below is written with :where().
127:    `font: inherit` at (0,1,1) outranks every Tailwind font utility (0,1,0), so
128:    a button carrying `text-[13px] font-black` inside this frame rendered at the
129:    inherited 16px/500 instead — which is what the Messages stage is full of.
130:    Family and style stay at reset strength (that is the part a reset is for:
131:    form controls otherwise default to Arial); the metrics a component may
132:    legitimately state for itself drop to (0,0,1), so a bare control still
133:    inherits and a stated size, weight, or leading now wins. */
134: .classroom-root button,
135: .classroom-root input,
136: .classroom-root textarea {
137:   font-family: inherit;
138:   font-style: inherit;
139:   font-variant: inherit;
140: }
141: 
142: :where(.classroom-root) :is(button, input, textarea) {
143:   font-size: inherit;
144:   font-weight: inherit;
145:   line-height: inherit;
146: }
